{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-hab-3-1","title":"Habakkuk 3:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Habakkuk, in his prayer, trembles at God's majesty. 17 The confidence of his faith.</p>\n<p>prayer. Ps 86:1-17; *title Ps 90:1-17; *title upon Shigionoth. or, according to variable songs, or tunes,called in Hebrew, Shigionoth. Ps 7:1-17; *title</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-2","title":"Habakkuk 3:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I have. 16; 1:5-10; Ex 9:20,21; 2Ch 34:27,28; Job 4:12-21; Ps 119:120 Isa 66:2; Jer 36:21-24; Da 8:17; Heb 11:7; 12:21; Re 15:4 speech. Heb. report, or hearing. Isa 53:1; Ro 10:16 O Lord. Ezr 9:8; Ps 85:6; 90:13-17; 138:7,8; Isa 51:9-11; 63:15-19; 64:1-4 Ho 6:2,3; Joh 10:10; Php 1:6 revive. or, preserve alive. in the. Jer 25:11,12; 52:31-34; Da 9:2 in wrath. Ex 32:10-12; Nu 14:10-23; 16:46,47; 2Sa 24:10-17; Ps 6:1,2; 38:1 Ps 78:38; Jer 10:24; 29:10; La 3:32; Zec 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-3","title":"Habakkuk 3:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>came. Jud 5:4,5; Ps 68:7,8; Isa 64:3 from. Ge 36:11; Jer 49:7; Am 1:12; Ob 1:9 Teman. or, the south. Paran. Ge 21:21; Nu 10:12; De 33:2; 1Sa 25:1 Selah. Ps 3:2,4; 4:4; 9:16,20 His glory. Ex 19:16-20; 20:18; 24:15-17; De 5:24; Ps 68:17; 114:3-7 and the earth. Isa 6:3; 2Co 3:7-11; Re 5:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-4","title":"Habakkuk 3:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>brightness. Ex 13:21; 14:20; Ne 9:12; Ps 104:2; Isa 60:19,20; Mt 17:2; 1Ti 6:16 Re 21:23; 22:5 horns coming out of his hand. or, bright beams out of hisside. the hiding. Job 26:14; Pr 18:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-5","title":"Habakkuk 3:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>went. Ex 12:29,30; Nu 14:12; 16:46-49; Ps 78:50,51; Na 1:2,3 and. Ps 18:7-13 burning coals. or, burning diseases. De 32:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-6","title":"Habakkuk 3:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>and measured. Ex 15:17; 21:31; Nu 34:1-29; De 32:8; Ac 17:26 and drove. Jos 10:42; 11:18-23; Ne 9:22-24; Ps 135:8-12 the everlasting. 10; Ge 49:26; De 33:15; Jud 5:5; Ps 68:16; 114:4-7; Isa 64:1-3 Na 1:5; Zec 14:4,5 his. Ps 90:2; 103:17; Isa 51:6,8; Mic 5:8; Mt 24:35; Lu 1:50; Heb 13:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-7","title":"Habakkuk 3:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>saw the. Ex 15:14-16; Nu 22:3,4; Jos 2:10; 9:24 Cushan. or, Ethiopia. Ge 10:6,7 in affliction. or, under affliction, or vanity. Midian. Ge 25:1-4; Nu 31:2-12; Ps 83:5-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-8","title":"Habakkuk 3:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the Lord. Ex 14:21,22; Jos 3:16,17; Ps 114:3,5; Isa 50:2; Na 1:4; Mr 4:39 Re 16:12 ride. 15; De 33:26,27; Ps 18:10; 45:4; 68:4,17; 104:3; Isa 19:1; Re 6:2 Re 19:11,14 of salvation. or, were salvation.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-9","title":"Habakkuk 3:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>bow. De 32:23; Ps 7:12,13; 35:1-3; Isa 51:9,10; 52:10; La 2:4 according. Ge 15:18-21; 17:7,8; 22:16-18; 26:3,4; 28:13,14; Ps 105:8-11 Lu 1:72-75; Heb 6:13-18 Selah. 9; Ps 143:6 Thou. Ex 17:6; Nu 20:11; Ps 78:15,16; 105:41; 1Co 10:4 the earth with rivers. or, the rivers of the earth.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-10","title":"Habakkuk 3:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>mountains. 6; Ex 19:16-18; Jud 5:4,5; Ps 68:7,8; 77:18; 97:4,5; 114:4,6 Isa 64:1,2; Jer 4:24; Mic 1:4; Na 1:5; Mt 27:51; Re 6:14; 20:11 the overflowing. Ex 14:22-28; Jos 3:15,16; 4:18,23,24; Ne 9:11; Ps 18:15; 66:6 Ps 74:13-15; 77:16-19; 114:3-8; 136:13-15; Isa 11:15,16; 63:11-13 Heb 11:29; Re 16:12 the deep. Ps 65:13; 93:3; 96:11-13; 98:7,8; Isa 43:20; 55:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-11","title":"Habakkuk 3:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>sun. Jos 10:12,13; Isa 28:21; 38:8 habitation. Ps 19:4 at the light of thine arrows they went. or, thine arrowswalked in the light. Jos 10:11; Ps 18:12-14; 77:17,18; 144:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-12","title":"Habakkuk 3:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>didst march. Nu 21:23-35; Jos 6:1-12:24; Ne 9:22-24; Ps 44:1-3; 78:55; Ac 13:19 thresh. Jer 51:33; Am 1:3; Mic 4:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-13","title":"Habakkuk 3:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>wentest. Ex 14:13,14; 15:1,2; Ps 68:7,19-23 with. Ps 77:20; 89:19-21; 99:6; 105:15,26; Isa 63:11 thou woundedst. Ex 12:29,30; Jos 10:11,24,42; 11:8,12; Ps 18:37-45; 68:21; 74:13,14 Ps 110:6 discovering. Heb. making naked.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-14","title":"Habakkuk 3:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the head. Ex 11:4-7; 12:12,13,29,30; 14:17,18; Ps 78:50,51; 83:9-11 they. Ex 14:5-9; 15:9,10; Ps 83:2,8; 118:10-12; Ac 4:27,28 came out. Heb. were tempestuous. Da 11:40; Zec 9:14 their. Ex 1:10-16,22; Ps 10:8; 64:2-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-15","title":"Habakkuk 3:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>walk. 8; Ps 77:19 heap. or, mud.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-16","title":"Habakkuk 3:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>I heard. 2; 1:5-11 my belly. Ps 119:120; Jer 23:9; Eze 3:14; Da 8:27; 10:8 that I. Ps 91:15; 94:12,13; Isa 26:20,21; Jer 15:10,11; 45:3-5; Eze 9:4-6 2Th 1:6-9 he will. 1:6; De 28:49-52; 2Ki 24:1,2; Jer 25:9-11 invade them. or cut them in pieces.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-17","title":"Habakkuk 3:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>the fig-tree. De 28:15-18,30-41; Jer 14:2-8; Joe 1:10-13,16-18; Am 4:6-10 Hag 2:16,17 fail. Heb. lie.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-18","title":"Habakkuk 3:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>I will rejoice. De 12:18; 1Sa 2:1; Job 13:15; Ps 33:1; 46:1-5; 85:6; 97:12; 104:34 Ps 118:15; 149:2; Isa 41:16; 61:10; Zec 10:7; Lu 1:46,47; Ro 5:2,3 Php 4:4; Jas 1:2,9,10; 1Pe 1:8; 4:12,13 the God. Ex 15:2; Ps 25:5; 27:1; 118:14; Isa 12:2; Mic 7:7; Lu 2:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-3-19","title":"Habakkuk 3:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>my strength. Ps 18:1; 27:1; 46:1; Isa 12:2; 45:24; Zec 10:12; 2Co 12:9,10 Eph 3:16; Php 4:13; Col 1:11 like. 2Sa 22:34; Ps 18:33 to walk. De 32:13; 33:29; Isa 58:14 stringed instruments. Heb. Neginoth. Ps 4:1-8; 6:1-10; 54:1-7; 55:1-23; 67:1-7; 76:1-12; *titles</p>"}]}